  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 4, L = 10, P = 22. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[7, 0, 16, 13, 7, 13, 18, 0, 17, 12], [1, 6, 18, 9, 16, 18, 10, 11, 15, 19], [3, 6, 6, 12, 5, 10, 19, 17, 11, 12], [8, 16, 18, 12, 3, 19, 8, 3, 4, 16]], sigma = [4, 3, 8, 1, 0, 9, 7, 6, 2, 5], B = [7, 4, 8, 4, 7, 17, 16, 16, 8, 17].",
